Fixes for the FaceTime plugin, @openclaw/facetime 2026.9.6 and 2026.9.7 (OpenClaw, MIT).

1. Calls end. On macOS 27 the last status the helper reports after a hangup
   is 6 (disconnected), with no end date, so the plugin never saw the call
   end and refused every new call until a gateway restart. Status 6 now
   counts as ended.
2. Tool work finishes. A repeat consult from the voice with no new caller
   speech (often the voice hearing itself) cancelled the check in progress,
   so its answer never arrived. Repeats are ignored until the caller says
   something new.
3. No talking to itself. The far end sent Uno's own voice back, and the
   voice took it for the caller: it cut itself off mid-sentence and answered
   itself in a loop. While Uno's voice plays, and for a second after, the
   caller's audio reaches the model as silence, unless it's well above the
   echo predicted from what Uno just said (the call's echo level is learned
   from the first 3 s of Uno's speech): then it's the caller talking over
   Uno, and it goes through. Each of Uno's turns logs an "echo gate" line
   with the levels.
4. Work survives a hang-up. Hanging up cancelled the agent's run, so a task
   asked for on the call (and its text) died with it. The run now finishes;
   only its spoken answer is dropped.
5. Bye, not a hang-up. The voice ended the call the moment the caller said
   they were going to hang up. Now it says bye and lets them hang up, and
   ends the call only when asked to, after saying bye.
6. The greeting: by name, the way a friend picks up, no self-introduction.
7. The audio driver builds with Xcode 27 (deployment target 12.0; the
   installer's pinned digest is updated to match).
8. No leftover audio capture. A call whose end couldn't be confirmed keeps
   its facetime-audio-capture running on purpose (fail-closed); after a
   gateway restart it was orphaned for good, ~15% of a core each (six of
   them from Oct 1 ran for a day). When a call ends with FaceTime's carrier
   confirmed closed, captures an earlier gateway left behind (parent is
   launchd) are stopped, logged as "stopped N leftover audio capture".

Apply after every install or update of the plugin, then restart the gateway:

  cd "$(openclaw plugins inspect facetime --json | node -pe 'JSON.parse(require("fs").readFileSync(0)).plugin.rootDir')"
  patch -p1 < ~/uno/patches/facetime-2026.9.6.patch

